WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.171 --> 00:00:01.899
- I want my baby-back-baby-back-baby-back.

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:04.331
♫ Chili's baby back ribs

00:00:04.331 --> 00:00:06.944
No one, not myself, no one
at Chili's, heard the piece

00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:08.651
of music after it was
done and thought this

00:00:08.651 --> 00:00:10.304
is going to be around for 20 years.

00:00:10.304 --> 00:00:13.485
I thought it'd be gone after six weeks.

00:00:13.485 --> 00:00:16.735
♫ I got my baby back ribs

00:00:16.735 --> 00:00:17.889
- [Man] Yeah, if you
want, you can have one.

00:00:17.889 --> 00:00:19.862
- Yeah, you know, I haven't eaten one.

00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:21.029
Why start now?

00:00:23.478 --> 00:00:25.121
My name is Guy Bommarito.

00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:27.414
I'm an Advertising Creative
Director and Copywriter,

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:29.694
and the one responsible for the Chili's

00:00:29.694 --> 00:00:31.763
Baby Back Ribs jingle.

00:00:31.763 --> 00:00:32.873
Barbecue sauce.

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:34.974
Most everybody's grown up with jingles

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:37.001
and I guess the older
you are the more jingles

00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:38.793
you remember because it
used to be, you know,

00:00:38.793 --> 00:00:41.747
the heart and soul of the entire industry.

00:00:41.747 --> 00:00:44.051
And so by the '90s when
this song was written,

00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:46.355
jingles had gotten to
a point where they were

00:00:46.355 --> 00:00:48.990
the lowest common denominator
form of advertising

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.155
and everybody avoided
them 'cause they were

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:53.988
typically annoying and, uh, um, unpleasant.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.822
We did it because the
client insisted on it.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.430
We never would have done it otherwise.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.254
I was so embarrassed
to take the assignment

00:01:00.254 --> 00:01:02.899
back to my creative department
that I just wrote it myself.

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:04.937
♫ Doo-Doo-Doo-Doo-Doo-Doo

00:01:04.937 --> 00:01:07.785
♫ I want my baby back ribs

00:01:07.785 --> 00:01:10.654
People would either say
that's my favorite song,

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:12.670
I love it, or they would
say if I hear that song

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.049
one more time I'm going
to stick a fork in my eye.

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:16.646
When the song first started taking off,

00:01:16.646 --> 00:01:18.707
my biggest concern was, “I hope that's not

00:01:18.707 --> 00:01:20.521
the only thing in my obituary.”

00:01:20.521 --> 00:01:22.601
I hope that I do something else, you know,

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:24.542
that surpasses that.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:25.961
Because I really don't want to be known

00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:29.294
as the guy that did Baby Back Ribs song.

